{
  "title": "Vegetarian Nutrition Plan Creation",
  "content": "## Plan Overview\n\nCreate a comprehensive vegetarian nutrition plan for a 155 lb moderately active individual targeting 2000-2200 cal/day, 120g protein, strength training 4x/week. The plan covers macro distribution, meal templates, snack rules, grocery staples, and MyFitnessPal setup.\n\n### Approach\n- **Parallel research**: Simultaneously develop the protein strategy/macro framework, meal templates, and research MyFitnessPal best practices for vegetarian tracking\n- **Synthesis**: Combine all components into a cohesive, actionable nutrition plan\n\n### Key Constraints\n- No seitan, no mushrooms, no regular milk/excess cheese\n- Greek yogurt and cottage cheese are OK despite mild dairy sensitivity\n- Preferred proteins: eggs, Greek yogurt, cottage cheese, legumes, tofu, occasional tempeh\n- 3 meals + 1-2 snacks structure",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "goal": "Design the macro framework and protein strategy: Calculate optimal macro split (protein/carbs/fat) for 2000-2200 cal with 120g protein target supporting muscle gain. Map out how to hit 120g protein daily using eggs, Greek yogurt, cottage cheese, legumes, tofu, and tempeh — including specific portion sizes and protein content per serving. Create protein distribution across meals (e.g., 30-40g per meal + snacks). Account for dairy sensitivity constraints.",
      "tool_name": "reasoning",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Research current best practices for vegetarian meal prep and high-protein vegetarian recipes that use eggs, Greek yogurt, cottage cheese, legumes, and tofu (excluding mushrooms and seitan). Find practical, time-efficient meal ideas suitable for busy schedules.",
      "tool_name": "web_search",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Research MyFitnessPal setup best practices for vegetarian tracking: how to set custom macro targets (2000-2200 cal, 120g protein), recommended barcode scanning tips for vegetarian products, how to create custom meals/recipes, best food logging strategies for legumes/tofu/eggs, and any vegetarian-specific tracking pitfalls to avoid.",
      "tool_name": "web_search",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Using the macro framework from Task 0 and meal research from Task 1, create detailed meal templates for breakfast, lunch, dinner, and 1-2 snacks. Each template should include: specific ingredients with portions, calorie and macro breakdown per meal, 2-3 variations per meal slot, and snack rules (what qualifies as a good snack, portion guidelines, protein minimums per snack). Also compile a comprehensive weekly grocery staples list organized by category (produce, dairy, pantry, frozen, etc.).",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": [0, 1]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Synthesize everything into the final comprehensive vegetarian nutrition plan document. Combine: (1) Macro framework and protein strategy from Task 0, (2) Meal templates, snack rules, and grocery staples from Task 3, (3) MyFitnessPal setup guide from Task 2. Format as a clean, actionable plan with sections: Overview & Targets, Daily Macro Breakdown, Protein Strategy, Meal Templates (with variations), Snack Rules, Weekly Grocery Staples List, and MyFitnessPal Setup & Tracking Guide. Include practical tips for adherence and meal prep.",
      "tool_name": "reasoning",
      "depends_on": [2, 3]
    }
  ],
